1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,470
Selling more than you hold costs money and trust.

2
00:00:04,470 --> 00:00:10,150
This video shows why the Inventory module exists, how counts, locations and purchase

3
00:00:10,150 --> 00:00:13,620
orders fit together, and how to use every screen.

4
00:00:18,220 --> 00:00:23,140
Nothing disappoints a shopper like paying for something that is not there.

5
00:00:23,140 --> 00:00:27,630
Selling more than you hold means refunds, apologies and lost trust.

6
00:00:28,380 --> 00:00:32,886
Counting stock by hand means a spreadsheet that is never quite right, and

7
00:00:32,886 --> 00:00:35,510
no warning before a bestseller runs out.

8
00:00:36,260 --> 00:00:41,506
The Inventory module counts every product and variant, holds units while a buyer

9
00:00:41,506 --> 00:00:44,800
pays, and takes them off when the order is paid.

10
00:00:45,550 --> 00:00:49,607
It tells you when stock is low, helps you order more from suppliers,

11
00:00:49,607 --> 00:00:51,690
and shows shoppers what is left.

12
00:00:55,890 --> 00:01:00,001
The Inventory part on a product type switches counting on.

13
00:01:00,001 --> 00:01:04,240
Commerce, Inventory lists every counted product and variant.

14
00:01:04,990 --> 00:01:09,772
A line is changed by receiving stock, adjusting it, or counting it, and

15
00:01:09,772 --> 00:01:12,070
its history keeps every change.

16
00:01:12,820 --> 00:01:15,927
Locations keep stock in more than one place.

17
00:01:15,927 --> 00:01:20,960
Purchase orders order from suppliers and receive the stock into a location.

18
00:01:21,710 --> 00:01:28,050
Settings, Commerce, Inventory sets the low-stock threshold, how long stock is held, and

19
00:01:28,050 --> 00:01:30,640
who is told when stock runs low.

20
00:01:34,818 --> 00:01:39,436
Stock is counted for content types that have the Inventory part.

21
00:01:39,436 --> 00:01:45,308
Open Content, Content Definition, Content Types, edit Product, and click Add Parts.

22
00:01:45,759 --> 00:01:47,902
Tick Inventory, and add it.

23
00:01:47,902 --> 00:01:51,279
Every product of this type can now be counted.

24
00:01:51,729 --> 00:01:55,788
Open Commerce, Inventory, and click Find products to count.

25
00:01:55,788 --> 00:01:59,409
Every product gets a line, with nothing on hand yet.

26
00:02:03,610 --> 00:02:07,921
Each line shows what is On hand, what is Reserved for orders being

27
00:02:07,921 --> 00:02:12,173
paid for, and what is Available, which is on hand minus reserved.

28
00:02:12,173 --> 00:02:14,030
Open a line to change it.

29
00:02:14,480 --> 00:02:17,850
Received records stock that arrived, such as a delivery.

30
00:02:17,850 --> 00:02:20,840
Enter how many came in, and a reason if you like.

31
00:02:21,290 --> 00:02:25,612
Adjusted records a correction up or down, such as damaged units.

32
00:02:25,612 --> 00:02:29,810
Enter a negative number to take stock away, and give a reason.

33
00:02:30,261 --> 00:02:32,658
Count records how many you counted.

34
00:02:32,658 --> 00:02:37,391
The count replaces what is on hand, and the history records the difference.

35
00:02:37,842 --> 00:02:42,446
The history lists every change, newest first, with what it was, the change,

36
00:02:42,446 --> 00:02:44,493
and what was on hand after it.

37
00:02:44,493 --> 00:02:48,302
Recount from history recomputes the number from that history.

38
00:02:52,495 --> 00:02:58,072
Export CSV downloads every counted product, with its SKU and how many are

39
00:02:58,072 --> 00:03:00,754
on hand, reserved and available.

40
00:03:00,754 --> 00:03:06,825
To set many counts at once, such as after a stocktake, change the OnHand column.

41
00:03:07,279 --> 00:03:11,585
Click Import CSV, choose the file, and click Import.

42
00:03:11,585 --> 00:03:16,114
Only OnHand is read, and each line is found by its SKU.

43
00:03:16,114 --> 00:03:20,049
If any line has a problem, nothing is imported.

44
00:03:24,243 --> 00:03:28,617
On a product's editor, the Inventory section sets how its stock is kept.

45
00:03:28,617 --> 00:03:32,263
Count stock stops counting the product when it is unticked.

46
00:03:32,717 --> 00:03:36,018
Allow backorders keeps selling when none are left.

47
00:03:36,018 --> 00:03:40,733
Low-stock threshold says when stock counts as low, and Ships from sets the

48
00:03:40,733 --> 00:03:43,327
date of a product that is not out yet.

49
00:03:43,779 --> 00:03:48,308
Below the settings, On hand lists each variant with how many are available,

50
00:03:48,308 --> 00:03:51,439
and a Change button that opens it under Inventory.

51
00:03:55,633 --> 00:04:01,704
Settings, Commerce, Inventory sets the Low-stock threshold for products without their own, and

52
00:04:01,704 --> 00:04:06,743
Hold stock for, the minutes units stay held for a buyer who has not paid yet.

53
00:04:07,195 --> 00:04:11,407
Notify about low stock chooses the roles whose users are told when a

54
00:04:11,407 --> 00:04:13,455
product runs low or sells out.

55
00:04:13,908 --> 00:04:18,247
Under Locations, fill in Add a location with a Name, such as Main

56
00:04:18,247 --> 00:04:21,181
warehouse, and an Address, and click Save.

57
00:04:21,181 --> 00:04:24,298
Stock can now be kept in more than one place.

58
00:04:24,748 --> 00:04:29,179
With more than one location, an item lists its stock By location, and

59
00:04:29,179 --> 00:04:33,728
Move between locations moves available units from one place to another.

60
00:04:37,929 --> 00:04:42,491
Commerce, Purchase orders keeps the stock you order from suppliers.

61
00:04:42,491 --> 00:04:44,429
Click Add purchase order.

62
00:04:44,879 --> 00:04:50,143
Enter the Supplier and the Supplier's email, where to Receive at, and when it is Expected.

63
00:04:50,143 --> 00:04:53,706
Leave the box to start with the items that are low on stock

64
00:04:53,706 --> 00:04:55,899
ticked, and click Start the order.

65
00:04:56,350 --> 00:05:00,912
Under Add items, Find items to order searches by SKU or name.

66
00:05:00,912 --> 00:05:05,473
Set how many are Ordered and the Unit cost of each, and save.

67
00:05:05,473 --> 00:05:10,170
Then click Mark as ordered, and the items can no longer change.

68
00:05:10,620 --> 00:05:15,609
When the stock arrives, enter what came under Arrived now, and click Receive

69
00:05:15,609 --> 00:05:18,164
what arrived, or Receive everything.

70
00:05:18,164 --> 00:05:22,240
The units go on hand, and each item's history shows Received.

71
00:05:26,503 --> 00:05:28,559
Shoppers see the stock on the shop.

72
00:05:28,559 --> 00:05:31,967
A product that is running low shows how many are left, and one

73
00:05:31,967 --> 00:05:34,423
that is gone shows that it is out of stock.

74
00:05:34,982 --> 00:05:38,652
The In stock filter lists only the products that can be bought now.

75
00:05:42,852 --> 00:05:44,055
A small shop:

76
00:05:44,055 --> 00:05:49,692
count what you hold, get a notification when a bestseller runs low, and order more.

77
00:05:50,442 --> 00:05:52,468
A shop and a warehouse:

78
00:05:52,468 --> 00:05:56,032
two locations, with stock moved between them.

79
00:05:56,782 --> 00:05:58,010
A stocktake:

80
00:05:58,010 --> 00:06:02,922
export the counts, correct the OnHand column, and import the file.

81
00:06:03,672 --> 00:06:04,599
A launch:

82
00:06:04,599 --> 00:06:10,222
Ships from and Allow backorders let shoppers pre-order a product that is not out yet.

83
00:06:12,222 --> 00:06:16,358
Count what you hold, change it with a reason, order more before it

84
00:06:16,358 --> 00:06:19,058
runs out, and show shoppers what is left.

85
00:06:19,058 --> 00:06:20,552
Thanks for watching.

